          "distinct": true,
          "id": "28fd66aeb63a7e227eebb094db0227f3674b1aa8",
          "message": "fix(zk/xpath): string.nr semantics — substring window, logical length, codepoint STRLEN (sq-3x7dl.6) [FABLE-5] (#1495)\n\n* fix(zk/xpath): string.nr semantics — substring window, logical length, codepoint STRLEN (sq-3x7dl.6) [FABLE-5]\n\nBUG A (audit HIGH): fn:substring clamped start to position 1 but still\nemitted `length` chars. Per F&O 5.4.3 the result is the chars at 1-based\npositions p with round(start) <= p < round(start) + round(length): a\nstart below 1 consumes part of the length budget. The inline test\ntest_substring_start_clamped enshrined the wrong answer (asserted\nsubstring(\"hello\",-2,4)==\"hell\"); replaced by\ntest_substring_start_below_one_consumes_length asserting \"h\". The raw\nstart is clamped into [-(2^32), N+1] before the window arithmetic so\nextreme i64 starts cannot overflow (both clamps preserve the result).\n\nBUG B (audit MEDIUM): ends_with anchored the suffix at the buffer\nCAPACITY (N-M); compare/string_equal/less/greater/le/ge tie-broke on\ncapacities; codepoint_equal gated on N==M. All now derive logical\nlengths (bytes up to the first NUL, mirroring hash.nr::logical_len), so\nSTRENDS(\"hello\" in str<10>,\"llo\") is true and equal content in str<10>\nvs str<3> is equal/codepoint-equal. NUL is a terminator, never U+0000\ncontent. Dynamic suffix reads are index-clamped for the post-flatten\nalways-executed read (same pattern as the sq-y73 translate fix).\n\nBUG C (audit MEDIUM): string_length counted non-NUL BYTES; fn:string-\nlength/STRLEN counts CODEPOINTS. Now counts UTF-8 lead bytes\n((b & 0xC0) != 0x80) up to the first NUL. Codepoints (not grapheme\nclusters) per F&O; ill-formed UTF-8 is not detected (documented).\n\nOracle (independent Python over the F&O window/collation definitions):\n  substring('hello',2,3)='ell'; substring('hello',-2,4)='h';\n  substring('12345',0,3)='12'; substring('12345',-3,5)='1';\n  substring('hello',1,10)='hello'; substring('hello',7,3)='';\n  substring('hello',3,0)=''; substring('hello',-100,3)='';\n  'hello'.endswith('llo')=True; endswith('')=True;\n  cmp('ab','ab')=0; cmp('ab','abc')=-1;\n  len('é')=1 (UTF-8 bytes [195,169]); len('aé')=2.\n\nMutation spot-checks (throwaway copy, each fix reverted in isolation):\n  substring window revert -> 3 tests FAIL; ends_with capacity-anchor\n  revert -> 2 FAIL; compare capacity tie-break revert -> 1 FAIL;\n  codepoint_equal N==M revert -> 1 FAIL; string_length byte-count\n  revert -> 2 FAIL. All restored clean.\n\nnargo 1.0.0-beta.21 (pinned): xpath lib 119 pass (46 string-scoped),\nxpath_unit_tests 281 pass; real test_packages run CI-style (stub +\nplaceholder exclusion, KNOWN_FAILING skips) — counts in the PR body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(zk/xpath): substring position-unit caveat — byte-window vs codepoint STRLEN composition trap (verify follow-up, sq-3x7dl.6) [FABLE-5]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
