          "distinct": true,
          "id": "cbfb2241d2a4e8ca645164b1922b07d21f298d40",
          "message": "fix(engine): kind-first total order for compare_terms — restores transitivity (sq-wjl8i) [FABLE-5] (#1502)\n\n* fix(engine): kind-first total order for compare_terms — restores transitivity (sq-wjl8i) [FABLE-5]\n\nThe SPARQL value comparator (`compare_terms` / the engine's `compare_values`,\nORDER BY + MIN/MAX fallback) was intransitive — three machine-checked\nwitnesses: the 2^53 double-collapse making a mixed exact/inexact triple\nEqual/Equal/Less, the `10 / \"11\" / 2` mixed-kind lexical cycle, and NaN\nmapped to `None` then to engine `Equal`. Fix: literals order KIND-FIRST by a\nfixed `LiteralKind` rank; value order only WITHIN a kind (exact-rational\nnumeric with the mixed-tier f64-tie recheck via `Num::cmp_total`, NaN\ntotalised first, dateTime/date by timeline, else lexical). Relational\n`<` / `=` (`num_compare` / XPath promotion) semantics are UNTOUCHED — only\nthe ORDER BY total order is refined in the region SPARQL leaves undefined.\n\nRecovery-completion verification (Opus 4.8, all evidence regenerated):\n- clippy -D warnings + tests GREEN in both feature states — sparq-substrate\n  (default / compare,numeric), sparq-reason (default / substrate-compare),\n  sparq-engine (371 tests).\n- Kani: `transitivity_mixed_literal_kinds_incl_nan` + 3 witness harnesses\n  + 2 domain-vacuity guards — Complete, 6 verified, 0 failures; the\n  kind-rank-revert mutation drives the witness harness + unit tests RED.\n- W3C SPARQL conformance delta vs origin/main = 0 (1225 pass / 0 fail /\n  4 documented divergence / 0 skip on both). rustdoc --all-features clean.\n\nRebased onto origin/main; the WIP commit's accidental absolute-path\n`tests/w3c` symlink is dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(bench): re-pin feature_off_exact for the compare_terms fix wasm growth (sq-wjl8i) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe kind-first total-order fix adds real feature-OFF engine code the wasm\nbundle links in (cmp_exact_lex_f64 / f64_exact_decimal / Num::cmp_total\ndecimal-string arithmetic + NaN totalisation), a legitimate +5042-byte\n(+0.360%) growth. Scalar arithmetic, NOT vectorization — the feature-OFF\nzero-delta invariant is preserved; only the absolute pin moves. Floor\n(1399703) unchanged (within its +2% band). CI-measured value from run\n28722406953.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bench): restore closing `]` of perf-baseline comment array (sq-wjl8i) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe e329efdb re-pin of feature_off_exact (1399868 -> 1404910, the correct\nCI-measured value) accidentally DELETED the closing `],` of the wasm_bundle_bytes\ncomment array, leaving `bench/perf-baseline.json` as INVALID JSON. The\nartifact-exact-equality leg2 then failed not on the byte comparison (measured\n1404910 == pinned 1404910) but on the JSON parse: \"Expecting ',' delimiter:\nline 93\". Re-adding the `],` restores valid JSON; leg2 now reports\n\"exact match: 1404910 == 1404910 (zero delta)\". Value and diagnosis unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
