          "distinct": false,
          "id": "dbc08e85ffe77a312dd33460327f62b9241513a8",
          "message": "feat(ci): wire per-merge incremental PKG ingest workflow (sq-tzars.4) (#1522)\n\n* feat(ci): wire per-merge incremental PKG ingest workflow (sq-tzars.4) [HAIKU-4.5]\n\nAdds .github/workflows/pkg-ingest.yml: triggers on push to main with\npath-filter (KB-relevant inputs) + workflow_dispatch, runs the deterministic\ningest_pkg.py, validates output against SHACL shapes via new validate-pkg\nbinary, uploads quarantine sidecar + generated TTL as artifacts, fails\nclosed on nonconformance. Post-merge only (never gates PRs); concurrency\ngroup prevents piling up.\n\nAlso adds crates/sparq-kb/src/bin/validate_pkg.rs (simple validator binary,\nrequired-features=[\"validate\"]) to support the workflow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): validate_pkg binary feature guard — cfg blocks inside main() [HAIKU-4.5]\n\nFix invalid Rust code: multiple main() functions with \\#[cfg] guards are not\nallowed. Move the feature guards inside a single main() function body.\n\n* fix(sparq-kb): clippy::get_first in validate_pkg bin — args.get(0) → args.first() (sq-tzars.4) [SONNET-4.6]\n\nFixes the clippy -D warnings failure on all four feature-matrix legs (validate,\nquery, close, literature+validate) caused by the get_first lint on line 25 of\nvalidate_pkg.rs. Single-character change: args.get(0) → args.first().\n\nAll five CI states verified locally:\n  default (no features) — bin not compiled (required-features gate)\n  --features validate   — clippy clean, tests pass\n  --features query      — clippy clean, tests pass\n  --features close      — clippy clean, tests pass\n  --features literature,validate — clippy clean, tests pass\n\nsparq-kb has no coverage-floor entry; ratchet not applicable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(sparq-kb): code-span the <ttl-file> placeholder — rustdoc unclosed-HTML-tag under --all-features (sq-tzars.4) [FABLE-5]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-05T04:59:11Z",
